<title>PERU: Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.323 billion.</title>
<headline>Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.323 billion.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Friday its net international reserves had risen $13 million to $9.323 billion by April 16 from $9.310 billion the previous week.</p>
<p>Peru's reserves ended 1996 at $8.540 billion. The government estimates reserves will rise above $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>((-- Lima Newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
